That seems quite a nonsensical statement to me.  Not everything that you 
are not meant to do is cheating.  There are people with photographic 
memory.  They would keep the stuff in mind anyway; they were not meant 
to.  Do they cheat?

One might also argue that you were not meant to use spoilers, otherwise 
the guide book would already contain them.  So using spoilers is cheating?

Since I am the only player on my computer and since bones files are 
extremely rare for me (I am not dying often enough), I usually remember 
the character and know the most important items in the pile when I 
encounter a bones files.  Certainly I am not meant to have free 
identification of items in a bones file.  So knowing them nonetheless is 
cheating?

Cheating is trying to win by illegitimate means.  I don't consider 
enhancing my real-world memory by taking notes in the real world 
illegitimate.  (I do consider the strength of the attack of mind flayers 
illegitimate to some extent.  If they took away knowledge of a small 
number of items and of a capped number of levels, I would not even 
consider taking notes to avoid the cumbersome effects of amnesia.  But 
taking away a quarter of levels with every successful attack is insane. 
And it does not add anything to the basic difficulty or ease of the 
game, it just makes it more cumbersome.)

